; Flags: named on/off facts the game remembers - a relic lifted, a seal broken,
; a lever pulled somewhere else (docs/tool-refinement-plan.md Phase 4).
;
; Like quests, a catalog says what a flag IS. Whether it is ON is save state
; (WorldState::flags, by id), never here.
;
; Fields:
;   display   the flag's name, as the editor lists it.
;   dungeon   the dungeon it belongs to: its LOCAL flags. Absent = a WORLD flag,
;             true everywhere. Check warns when something in another dungeon
;             reads or writes a local one.
;
; What sets one: an item's `flag = <id>` when it is lifted, a lever's
; `sets=` / `toggles=` (and `clears=` turns one off). What reads one: a door's,
; a lever's or a stair's `flag=`, which waits until it is on, and a world-map
; location's `flag=`, whose doorway is barred until then.

